     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Use the following:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">  x &lt;- read.cross(&quot;csv&quot;, &quot;/powerplant/workspace/cfnnvt/rqtl/11_5&quot;,</span><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">                  &quot;rqtl_fam_11_5_format.csv&quot;,<br>                  genotypes=c(&quot;AC&quot;,&quot;AD&quot;,&quot;BC&quot;,&quot;BD&quot;), crosstype=&quot;4way&quot;) <br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"></span>- don&#39;t specify the alleles argument; that is not used for 4-way crosses, and can only be two alleles</div><div>- use the genotypes argument to specify the genotype codes that you are using in the file</div><div>- use the crosstype argument to specify the cross type</div><div><br></div><div>karl<br></div></div>"
    ],
